From 25a624aa0cc8d87921b14477d3bcdc564f44a5b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:15:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/23] doc/ac4enc: note CLI silent auto-fold, explicit-layout
 exit 234, immersive deferred

The ffmpeg CLI auto-downmixes >6ch inputs to 5.1 silently
(framework auto_aresample, upstream of the encoder); only an explicit
-channel_layout outside stereo/5.1 fails loud (exit 234). Immersive
(5.1.4/objects) encode is out of scope for this series.

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
---
 doc/encoders.texi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/encoders.texi b/doc/encoders.texi
index 6bf4ea8..feb8f0e 100644
--- a/doc/encoders.texi
+++ b/doc/encoders.texi
@@ -562,6 +562,12 @@ the loudness floor (use @code{loudness_target=0} to skip the
 correction gain). A streaming (low-memory) mode is planned but not
 implemented here.
 
+Inputs with more than 6 channels are silently downmixed to 5.1 by the
+framework's automatic resampling before the encoder sees them. Only an
+explicit @code{-channel_layout} outside stereo and 5.1 fails loudly
+(@samp{not supported by the ac4 encoder}, exit code 234). Immersive
+(5.1.4 and object-based) encoding is not implemented in this series.
+
